// THE version of the `bit` toolchain — the single source of truth. `bit`
// compiles this constant directly.
//
// Because the truth is checked in, a release tarball with no `.git` at all
// builds and reports the right version — nothing consults git, a tag, or the
// network.
//
// A RELEASE OVERRIDES IT BY STAGING, NOT BY A BUILD OPTION. `dist/release.sh`
// copies compiler/ to dist/out/stagesrc/compiler with this file EXCLUDED and a
// generated one in its place, then cross-builds the three targets from that
// copy. The working tree is never patched.
//
// There is no build-driver option that stamps this, and there should not be:
// release.sh's staging is the path a real release takes, and it needs three
// CROSS-built targets rather than the one native compiler a flag could stamp.
//
// Keep this one line in the shape `const bitVersion: string = "..."` and keep
// it the only such line in the file: release.sh greps for exactly that and
// refuses to build if it finds anything other than one match.
const bitVersion: string = "0.1.0-dev"
